---
/*
 * Vision — the argument behind Modesto.
 *
 * Built in Modesto's own editorial system (see /branding): hairline-bordered
 * sections with numbered kickers, large tight-tracked display type, and DM Mono
 * reserved for evidence. Every claim here is something the product does today.
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/ResourceLayout.astro";
import SquareMeter from "../components/SquareMeter.astro";

const providers = [
  "Claude Code", "Codex", "Cursor", "Antigravity", "Gemini", "Grok", "Factory Droid",
  "Kilo Code", "OpenCode", "Pi", "Devin", "Poolside", "Kimi", "Qwen",
];
---

<Layout
  title="Vision — Modesto"
  description="Agents multiplied. The work between them didn't. Why Modesto keeps the record instead of shipping another model."
>
  <section class="v-hero">
    <p class="mono">Modesto / Vision</p>
    <h1>Agents multiplied.<br />The work between<br />them didn't.</h1>
    <div class="v-hero-note">
      <span class="mono">09 / 2026</span>
      <p>Why the connective tissue between coding agents is the part worth owning.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-kicker"><span class="mono">01</span><span>The problem</span></div>
    <div class="v-split">
      <h2>Context evaporates<br />at every seam.</h2>
      <div class="v-copy">
        <p>
          Two years ago most people used one coding agent, if they used one at all. Now a
          working developer might keep Claude Code open for refactors, reach for Codex on a
          long migration, and let Cursor handle edit-in-place work — before a team has
          standardised on anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each of those tools is good. None of them has a memory of the others. Close a
          session and the reasoning is gone. Move a task between agents and you re-explain
          the constraints, the half-finished paths, the decision you already made and do
          not want revisited. The code survives. The context around it does not.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-kicker"><span class="mono">02</span><span>The bet</span></div>
    <div class="v-split">
      <h2>The record<br />is the product.</h2>
      <div class="v-copy">
        <p>
          We are not betting on which agent wins. There will keep being more of them and
          they will keep getting better. The durable thing is the connective tissue — what
          changed, what is unfinished, what was decided, and which agent should pick it up
          — and that should belong to you, on your machine, not to a vendor.
        </p>
        <div class="v-figure">
          <SquareMeter total={14} filled={14} columns={7} labels={providers} />
          <p class="mono">14 providers / 1 workspace / 0 servers in between</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section">
    <div class="v-kicker"><span class="mono">03</span><span>How it holds</span></div>
    <div class="v-evidence">
      <article>
        <h3>A checkpoint is a Git ref</h3>
        <p>Handing work between agents resolves to an orphan commit, so the next agent reads the tree — not a paraphrase of it.</p>
        <code class="mono">refs/modesto/agent-checkpoints/…</code>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>The graph is derived, not kept</h3>
        <p>Lineage is drawn from data already tracked on a thread, so it cannot quietly drift out of sync with the work.</p>
        <code class="mono">forkSourceThreadId · lastKnownPr</code>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Drivers and instances split</h3>
        <p>The same agent can be configured twice with separate credentials, and an unknown provider degrades instead of crashing.</p>
        <code class="mono">codex_work · codex_personal</code>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="v-section v-last">
    <div class="v-kicker"><span class="mono">04</span><span>What we won't do</span></div>
    <div class="v-split">
      <h2>No model.<br />No middleman.</h2>
      <div class="v-copy">
        <p>
          Modesto does not train a model, proxy your prompts, or hold your credentials.
          Authentication, billing, and limits stay with the provider you already pay. If
          Modesto disappeared tomorrow, your repositories and your history would be exactly
          where they already are.
        </p>
        <a class="v-link" href="/docs">Read how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .v-hero,
  .v-section {
    width: min(100% - 48px, var(--container));
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-inline: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .v-hero {
    padding: clamp(72px, 10vw, 150px) clamp(24px, 5vw, 76px) clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px);
  }

  .v-hero > .mono {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .v-hero h1 {
    margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px) 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 7.4vw, 6.4rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    line-height: 0.94;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .v-hero-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 30px;
    align-items: end;
  }

  .v-hero-note .mono {
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 10px;
  }

  .v-hero-note p {
    max-width: 430px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ── Numbered sections ── */
  .v-section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .v-last {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .v-kicker {
    height: 52px;
    padding: 0 clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .v-kicker .mono {
    font-size: 9px;
  }

  .v-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px);
    padding: clamp(44px, 6vw, 88px) clamp(24px, 5vw, 76px);
  }

  .v-split h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 0.98;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .v-copy p {
    max-width: 56ch;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .v-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  /* The square grid is a figure, not decoration: one cell per provider. */
  .v-figure {
    margin-top: 34px;
    padding-top: 26px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .v-figure .mono {
    margin-top: 16px;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* ── Evidence row ── */
  .v-evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .v-evidence article {
    padding: clamp(30px, 3.4vw, 46px) clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 34px);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .v-evidence article:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  .v-evidence h3 {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .v-evidence p {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .v-evidence code {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 20px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 11px;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .v-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .v-link:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .v-hero-note,
    .v-split,
    .v-evidence {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .v-evidence article {
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .v-evidence article:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
